{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "נפתלי אילה שלוחה", :translit "naphtali ayalah sheluchah", :gloss "Naphtali is a hind let loose"} {:he "אילה שלוחה", :translit "ayalah sheluchah", :gloss "a hind let loose"} {:he "דבורה", :translit "devorah", :gloss "Deborah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Feminine form 'hind' alludes to Deborah, a woman, who directed the battle from Naphtali's territory."}], :frame {:text "Judges 4:6–10 records that Deborah summoned Barak and commanded him to take ten thousand men from Naphtali and Zebulun to fight Sisera. Judges 4:14 states that Deborah said to Barak 'Arise, for this is the day.' Judges 5:1 introduces the Song of Deborah. The Ba'al HaTurim reads Jacob's blessing as a prophecy anticipating this battle, and explains the feminine noun 'hind' (אילה) as an allusion to Deborah.", :sources ["Judges 4:6–10" "Judges 4:14" "Judges 5:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "הנותן אמרי שפר", :translit "ha-noten imrei shefer", :gloss "who gives words of beauty"} {:he "אמרי שפר", :translit "imrei shefer", :gloss "words of beauty"} {:he "ותשר דבורה", :translit "vatashar devorah", :gloss "and Deborah sang"} {:he "שיר ושבחה", :translit "shir veshevachah", :gloss "song and her praise"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אמרי שפר", :b "שיר ושבחה"}], :frame {:text "Judges 5:1 states 'And Deborah and Barak son of Abinoam sang.' The phrase 'words of beauty' in Genesis 49:21 is read as an allusion to Deborah's song, and the gematria equation with 'song and her praise' reinforces this reading.", :sources ["Judges 5:1" "Genesis 49:21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אילה שלוחה הנותן אמרי שפר", :translit "ayalah sheluchah ha-noten imrei shefer", :gloss "a hind let loose, who gives words of beauty"} {:he "ותשר דבורה וברק בן אבינועם ביום ההוא", :translit "vatashar devorah u-varak ben avino'am ba-yom ha-hu", :gloss "and Deborah and Barak son of Abinoam sang on that day"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אילה שלוחה הנותן אמרי שפר", :b "ותשר דבורה וברק בן אבינועם ביום ההוא"}], :frame {:text "Judges 5:1 states 'And Deborah and Barak son of Abinoam sang on that day.' The Ba'al HaTurim shows that the entire phrase from Jacob's blessing over Naphtali in Genesis 49:21 carries a gematria equal to this verse, reinforcing the claim that Jacob's words prophesied Deborah and Barak's victory.", :sources ["Judges 5:1" "Genesis 49:21"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Feminine form 'hind' alludes to Deborah, a woman, who directed the battle from Naphtali's territory.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "אמרי שפר", :a-value 831, :b "שיר ושבחה", :b-value 831, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :gematria, :a "אילה שלוחה הנותן אמרי שפר", :a-value 1737, :b "ותשר דבורה וברק בן אבינועם ביום ההוא", :b-value 1737, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:12:32.817163048Z", :model "glm-5.2"}